cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Polypus in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Polypus: A Distributed Quantum Computing Library"
type: software
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-09-23
license: EUPL-1.2
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bahia-Software/polypus"
url: "https://bahia-software.github.io/polypus/"

abstract: >-
  Polypus is an open-source distributed quantum computing library. It runs
  quantum circuits and trains variational quantum algorithms (VQE, QAOA, QML)
  across one or many QPUs, simulated or real, without changing the circuit
  code. The core is written in Rust for performance and correctness, and
  Python bindings via PyO3 make it a drop-in accelerator for existing Qiskit
  workflows. Shot execution and population-based training are distributed
  across QPUs, and backends range from local simulation through Qiskit Aer to
  CESGA's CUNQA distributed QPU platform and CESGA's QMIO quantum processor.

keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - distributed computing
  - variational quantum algorithms
  - VQE
  - QAOA
  - quantum machine learning
  - high performance computing
  - Rust
  - QPU

